<sect2 id="plug-in-smooth-palette">
  <title>Paleta suave</title>

  <indexterm>
    <primary>Cores</primary>
    <secondary>Paleta suave</secondary>
  </indexterm>
  <indexterm>
    <primary>Paleta suave</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <sect3>
    <title>Visão geral</title>
    <figure>
      <title>Exemplo do filtro <quote>Paleta suave</quote></title>
      <mediaobject>
        <imageobject>
          <imagedata format="JPG" fileref="images/filters/examples/taj_orig.jpg"/>
        </imageobject>
        <caption>
          <para>Imagem original</para>
        </caption>
      </mediaobject>
      <mediaobject>
        <imageobject>
          <imagedata format="JPG" fileref="images/filters/examples/color-taj-smoothpalette.jpg"/>
        </imageobject>
        <caption>
          <para>Filtro <quote>Paleta suave</quote> aplicado</para>
        </caption>
      </mediaobject>
    </figure>
    <para>Este efeito cria uma paleta de faixas com cores da camada ativa ou seleção. O propósito principal deste filtro é criar um mapa de cores para ser usado com o filtro <link linkend="plug-in-flame">Chama</link>.</para>
    <note>
      <para>Este comando somente funciona em imagens RGB. Se a imagem estiver em Tons de Cinza ou for Indexada, a entrada no menu é desativada.</para>
    </note>
    </sect3>

  <sect3>
    <title>Activating the Command</title>
    <para>
      You can access this command from the main menu through
      <menuchoice>
        <guimenu>Colors</guimenu>
        <guisubmenu>Info</guisubmenu>
        <guimenuitem>Smooth Palette…</guimenuitem>
      </menuchoice>.
    </para>
  </sect3>

  <sect3>
    <title>Opções</title>
    <figure>
      <title>Opções da <quote>Paleta suave</quote></title>
      <mediaobject>
        <imageobject>
          <imagedata format="PNG" fileref="images/menus/colors/info/smoothpalette.png"/>
        </imageobject>
      </mediaobject>
    </figure>
    <variablelist>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Width</term>
        <term>Height</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            You can set palette dimensions for <guilabel>Width</guilabel> and
            <guilabel>Height</guilabel>. Dimensions are linked when the chain
            is not broken. You can also select the unit.
          </para>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Search depth</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Increasing Search depth (1 - 1024) will result in more shades in
            the palette.
          </para>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
  </sect3>
</sect2>
